content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive with the breakpoint name, such as `md`, inside your custom CSS. This is documented in `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, under "Using custom CSS → Using variants" (lines 299–400). The page's examples use `dark` and `hover`, not a breakpoint, but it says `@variant` applies any Tailwind variant. Breakpoints are variants too, so this should work:

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;

  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

The docs don't show a breakpoint example for `@variant`, so I haven't confirmed this exact snippet. Custom breakpoints come from `--breakpoint-*` theme variables (`src/docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Customizing your theme"). The `theme.mdx` section "Relationship to variants" says the same thing.

